{"slug": "74hc595-shift-register", "targets": ["ic 74hc595"], "html": "<h2 style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:700;color:#0186e0;margin:34px 0 16px;\">IC 74HC595 Pinout: All 16 Pins at a Glance</h2><p><strong>IC 74HC595</strong> is a 16 pin, 8 bit serial in parallel out shift register with an output latch, sold in DIP, SOIC and TSSOP packages. The six control pins are covered above; the table below lists every pin of the IC 74HC595 so you can wire the chip straight from the reference.</p><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\"><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:16px;\"><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Pin</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Name</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Function</th></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">1 to 7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">QB to QH (Q1 to Q7)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Parallel outputs 2 to 8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">GND</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Ground</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">QH' (Q7S)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Serial output, feeds SER of the next chip</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">SRCLR (MR)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Shift register clear, active low, tie to VCC for normal use</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">SRCLK (SHCP)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Shift clock, data moves on the rising edge</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">RCLK (STCP)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Latch clock, copies the byte to the outputs on the rising edge</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">OE</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Output enable, active low, tie to GND to keep outputs on</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">SER (DS)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Serial data input</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">QA (Q0)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Parallel output 1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">VCC</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Supply, 2 V to 6 V for the HC family</td></tr></table></div><h3 style=\"font-size:19px;font-weight:700;color:#1a2b4a;margin:20px 0 10px;\">Wiring Checklist</h3><ol><li>Connect VCC and GND and place a 0.1 µF decoupling capacitor close to pin 16.</li><li>Tie SRCLR high and OE low unless you need clear or blanking control.</li><li>Wire SER, SRCLK and RCLK to three microcontroller pins.</li><li>Fit a series resistor on each LED output and keep total chip current within the datasheet limit.</li><li>For more outputs, link QH' to SER of the next IC and share both clock lines.</li></ol>"}